    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8849" root="حلف" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلْفَةٌ</span></b>  <i>An oath.</i> (Msb, TA. *) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلَفَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلْفَةً</span>, (TA,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْلُوفَةً</span></b> , i. e. <i>He swore an
oath;</i> (Lth, K;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلَفَ أُحْلُوفَةً</span></b>  [which
means the same]: (Lh, TA:) this last word is
of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُفْعُولَة</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَلِفُ</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِلْفٌ</span>.

